media: sun50i-h713-hdmirx: repeat a failed first switch slowly and more than once

0128 repeated the first source switch the moment the firmware reported the
HDMI source again, with SetSource 1 and 3 back to back as the ordinary
switch sends them. Provoked on 08.09.2026 (source toggling HDMI during
boot): the repeat hit a port that had locked 50 ms earlier, the port fell
to state 3 and stayed there -- no relock, no SwitchState, no callback --
and the wall stayed on the console. A switch by hand with a second between
the two calls brought it back; so did nothing else.

So the repeat now waits two seconds after the callback for the firmware to
settle, pauses a second between away and back, gives the relock three
seconds, and if the capture still does not come tries again five seconds
later, five times at most, saying so each time. It also checks first
whether the firmware brought the capture back by itself meanwhile. The
ordinary switch of a first publication is unchanged: it meets a port that
has been locked for a while and has been measured to work.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-08 09:27:26.089705073 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-08 09:27:51.702534091 +0200
@@ -307,6 +307,21 @@
